   2:Core/Src/posture_controller.c **** The Algorithm
   3:Core/Src/posture_controller.c **** There should be a good_posture_vector that is representing the ideal posture
   4:Core/Src/posture_controller.c **** 
   5:Core/Src/posture_controller.c **** If the angle deviates more than x degrees for more than x seconds, then it should go into realign m
   6:Core/Src/posture_controller.c **** 
   7:Core/Src/posture_controller.c **** While in realign mode, it should vibrate. There should be x seconds between each vibration
   8:Core/Src/posture_controller.c **** 
   9:Core/Src/posture_controller.c **** If it is over the threshold by an unrealistic amount, it should not notify
  10:Core/Src/posture_controller.c **** 
  11:Core/Src/posture_controller.c **** If the posture returns under the threshold for more than x seconds, it should go back into good_pos
  12:Core/Src/posture_controller.c **** 
  13:Core/Src/posture_controller.c **** There should be a function for asking if the posture is good
  14:Core/Src/posture_controller.c **** 
  15:Core/Src/posture_controller.c **** Learning the good_posture_vector while correcting
  16:Core/Src/posture_controller.c **** There are two parameters that can be tuned, the good_posture_vector and the threshold
  17:Core/Src/posture_controller.c **** 
  18:Core/Src/posture_controller.c **** We can update/learn the good_posture_vector dynamically when the posture goes from bad to good.
  19:Core/Src/posture_controller.c **** If:
  20:Core/Src/posture_controller.c **** - the posture returns from bad to good
  21:Core/Src/posture_controller.c **** - it have been under the threshold for x seconds
  22:Core/Src/posture_controller.c **** - The max distance between any two out of the last x measurements are under x deg
  23:Core/Src/posture_controller.c **** This ensures that we know they corrected their posture, and that they are sitting still
  24:Core/Src/posture_controller.c **** Then update the good_posture_vector by moving it closer to the average of the last x measurements
  25:Core/Src/posture_controller.c **** 
  26:Core/Src/posture_controller.c **** Learning the good_posture_vector after device have been placed
  27:Core/Src/posture_controller.c **** If the device have just been placed on the body or if it have been taken off and placed again, the 
  28:Core/Src/posture_controller.c **** If we have remained outside the threshold for a very long time, we might assume that good_posture_v
  29:Core/Src/posture_controller.c **** If the angle is over threshold by an extreme amount for a long time, we can assume it is not valid 
  30:Core/Src/posture_controller.c **** If the user does not correct the posture when notified, we can assume that they are already at the 
  31:Core/Src/posture_controller.c **** 
  32:Core/Src/posture_controller.c **** The good_posture_vector should be reset if:
ARM GAS  /var/folders/bp/ytvqs5756l50d7lg2fzmjpcr0000gn/T//ccuY7655.s 			page 2


  33:Core/Src/posture_controller.c **** - It have been over the threshold for over x seconds
  34:Core/Src/posture_controller.c **** 
  35:Core/Src/posture_controller.c **** If it transitions from moving a lot mode to not moving a lot mode, then we don't want to notify the
  36:Core/Src/posture_controller.c **** 
  37:Core/Src/posture_controller.c **** Actually, if it have been moving a lot, then we want to recalibrate no matter what, so we will not 
  38:Core/Src/posture_controller.c **** 
  39:Core/Src/posture_controller.c **** Calibrate with button
  40:Core/Src/posture_controller.c **** If the button is pressed for more than 3 seconds, just recalibrate
  41:Core/Src/posture_controller.c **** 
